---
title: Cinnamon Sugar Speculoos Squares
source: https://tastecooking.com/recipes/cinnamon-sugar-speculoos-squares/
servings: 24
image: https://tastecooking.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/speculoos-squares_recipe-500x324.jpg
author: Jesse Szewczyk
---

> The source is just a repost of Cookies by Jesse Szewczyk. 

Preheat the oven to 325°F and position a rack in the middle. 

Line a #9 x 13-inch metal baking pan{} with parchment paper, leaving some overhang on the long sides for easy lifting after baking. Lightly coat the paper with pan spray.

In a large, microwave-safe bowl, combine @speculoos cookie butter{1/2%cup} and @butter{2%sticks}(unsalted, cut into ½-inch cubes). Microwave in 30-second increments, stirring between each, until completely melted, about ~{60-90%seconds} total. 

Add @brown sugar{2%cups} and whisk until smooth. 

Add @eggs{2}(room temperature) and @vanilla extract{1%tbsp} and whisk until smooth and ribbony.

Add @flour{2.5%cups}(spooned and leveled), @baking powder{1/2%tsp}, @baking soda{1/4%tsp}, @salt{3/4%tsp}, and @ground cinnamon{1/4%tsp}. Stir with a rubber spatula just until a soft dough forms with no pockets of dry flour. 

Transfer the dough to the prepared baking pan and press into an even layer using clean hands coated with pan spray.

Sprinkle @sugar{1%tbsp} over the top. Lightly press the sugar into the dough with your hands. 

Bake until the top is lightly browned and the edges are set, and a toothpick inserted into the center comes out clean, about ~{30-35%minutes}. 

Let cool at room temperature for at least ~{2%hours}.

== Glaze ==

> The original recipe calls for twice this amount, but we found that was too much glaze. YMMV.

In a medium bowl, whisk together @confectioners' sugar{3/8%cup} and @milk{10%mL}(1/2 tbsp plus 1/2 tsp) until smooth. Transfer half the glaze o a second medium bowl and add @speculoos cookie butter{1/2%tbsp} and @ground cinnamon{1/8%tsp}. Whisk until completely smooth, adding additional milk to thin it as needed. Both glazes should be thick yet pourable. If either of them is too thick, add additional @milk; if too thin, add additional confectioners' sugar.

Drizzle the top of the bars with the glazes and let set for ~{20%minutes}, then slice into 24 pieces (6 long rows by 4 short rows).

> The bars will keep in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 1 week.